  "prompt": "[Table 1]\n\nThe table shows several values of the function\n[Figure 2]\n. If\n[Figure 3]\nis a polynomial function of degree at most 3, what is the value of\n[Figure 4]\n?",
  "choices": {
    "A": "[Figure 5]",
    "B": "[Figure 6]",
    "C": "[Figure 7]",
    "D": "[Figure 8]"
  },
  "correctAnswer": "C",
  "explanation": "The pattern in the table can be modeled by $g(x) = x^3 + x^2$. Substituting each value: $g(1) = 1 + 1 = 2$, $g(2) = 8 + 4 = 12$, $g(3) = 27 + 9 = 36$, $g(4) = 64 + 16 = 80$, and $g(5) = 125 + 25 = 150$. All values match. Therefore, $g(6) = 6^3 + 6^2 = 216 + 36 = 252$.\n\nWhy A is incorrect:\n\nThis is the value of $6^3$ alone, which results from omitting the $x^2$ term in the function.",
